cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you used SlideScope to view, measure or annotate images in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SlideScope: desktop digital pathology and microscopy viewer"
authors:
  - name: "SlideScope"
    website: "https://slidescope.science/"
url: "https://slidescope.science/"
abstract: >-
  SlideScope is a desktop viewer for whole slide images and research microscopy files on
  Windows and macOS. It opens Aperio SVS, Hamamatsu NDPI, 3DHISTECH MRXS, Leica SCN,
  Ventana BIF, Akoya QPTIFF, DICOM WSI, ZEISS CZI, Nikon ND2, Leica LIF, Imaris IMS and
  TIFF/OME-TIFF files locally, with calibrated measurement, annotations, GeoJSON and
  OME-TIFF export, and side-by-side comparison.
keywords:
  - digital pathology
  - whole slide imaging
  - microscopy
  - image viewer
  - histology
  - SVS
  - NDPI
  - CZI
  - ND2
  - DICOM
  - OME-TIFF
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://bio.tools/slidescope"
    description: "bio.tools registry entry"
  - type: url
    value: "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q140797497"
    description: "Wikidata item"
